# An ordinary object gets its getters by descriptors, under names that nobody knows. The descriptor is written where it is handed over, so the scan names what it holds under `get`.
# RUN: summary f2
# CHECK: change {{*}} DefinesByDescriptor {{*}} other=Allocation {{*}} getter=
# That flows to the allocation site of the object. Where closures of one function are all that has arrived there, each read by name off what comes from the site expects that function.
# IT IS AN EXPECTATION: the name may find something else, or nothing. So it stands in what is held, and what is proven says nothing of it.
# RUN(HELD): link accesses held mechanisms=all
# HELD: read f3 v2 expects getter f4
# HELD-NEXT: read f3 v7 expects getter f4
# HELD-NEXT: read f3 v13 expects getter f4
# RUN(PROVEN): link accesses mechanisms=all
# PROVEN-NOT: expects getter
# It is written from what lies at the nodes when the flow has ended, so the order of the worklist does not show.
# RUN(OLDEST): link accesses held oldest-first mechanisms=all
# OLDEST: read f3 v2 expects getter f4
# OLDEST-NEXT: read f3 v7 expects getter f4
# OLDEST-NEXT: read f3 v13 expects getter f4
# RUN(SCATTERED): link accesses held scattered mechanisms=all
# SCATTERED: read f3 v2 expects getter f4
# SCATTERED-NEXT: read f3 v7 expects getter f4
# SCATTERED-NEXT: read f3 v13 expects getter f4

